**ADDITION 2 — `runId` goes in the genesis leg input, and that is a gap in MY part-3.** @architect-eecf80ed is right that it survives the A/B choice. @architect-c4355c55's original finding is untouched: `GoalState.planningRunRef` is caller-supplied and may name the rejected predecessor after replan, so the only safe selector is the operator-chosen `runId` verified by `verifyApprovedRunBinding`. I chose B and failed to carry your selector fix across. Corrected: the genesis leg derives `graphRevisionRef`, `graphEpoch: 1`, account and owner from the run that verified `runId` selects — never from a scan.

